WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:03.073
- Bless me, Lord, for I am going to sin.

00:00:03.073 --> 00:00:05.290
(choir music plays)

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:06.970
- [Narrator] Midnight Mass
is the latest addition

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:09.942
to writer-director, Mike
Flanagan's horror repertoire.

00:00:09.942 --> 00:00:12.550
(door creaks)

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:14.330
Let's take a look at how Midnight Mass

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:17.746
is connected to Hill House
and other Flanagan titles.

00:00:17.746 --> 00:00:19.870
(choir music plays)

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:22.000
Many fans have speculated
that, like the work

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.790
of one of Flanagan's role
models, Stephen King,

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.040
all of Flanagan's film
and television projects

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:30.100
are connected as part of a larger MFCU,

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.390
Mike Flanagan Cinematic Universe,

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:34.100
or the Flanaverse for short.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.520
The Haunting of Hill House
and The Hunting of Bly Manor

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:38.990
were both based on pieces
of classic literature:

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:42.080
Shirley Jackson's 1959 novel,
The Haunting of Hill House,

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:44.390
and Henry James' 1898 novella,

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:46.340
The Turning of The Screw, respectively.

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.810
Midnight Mass is separate
from The Haunting anthology

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:51.210
and is not based on classic literature.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:53.310
If you're a true MFCU fan,

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:55.430
you already know that
Flanagan makes reference

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:57.430
to Midnight Mass in two of his films,

00:00:57.430 --> 00:00:59.240
Hush and Gerald's Game.

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:03.420
(groans)

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:04.540
- Get the fuck away!

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:06.720
- I finished your book.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:10.320
What did I think? I loved Riley.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.600
I loved Erin. They were great.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:15.480
- [Narrator] Casting is
the most obvious connection

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:18.500
between Midnight Mass and
Flanagan's other productions.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:21.280
Kate Siegel, one of Flanagan's
most frequent collaborators

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.160
and wife, stars in the series.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:25.610
- Then city council, were
you will be, kind of,

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:28.427
but not really slut-shamed by Bev Keane.

00:01:28.427 --> 00:01:29.260
- Ah.

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:31.010
- Dad, don't give this woman our money.

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:33.070
(furniture rattles)

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:35.940
- I thought I told you not
to play around in here.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:38.180
- [Narrator] Henry Thomas,
another Flanaverse regular,

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:40.590
also plays an important role.

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:43.160
- So church isn't for you, huh?

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:45.870
- Well, I didn't know that
they were all gonna die.

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:47.410
- [Narrator] Several
other Flanagan favorites

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:48.610
grace Midnight Mass.

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:49.520
- They know that.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:50.770
- Let's calm down a bit.

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:53.000
- You be calm, Leigh. It's
not your name in here.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.560
- [Narrator] This includes Annabeth Gish.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:55.890
- Are you ready for this?

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:58.670
- Sarah Gunning. You're...

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:00.760
...I've heard about you, Father.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:01.980
- [Narrator] Rahul Kohli.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:05.650
- Was he afraid of it,
intrigued by it, or?

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:08.300
- Well, you have to warn me, don't you?

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:09.950
You have to help me.

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:11.150
- [Narrator] Alex Essoe.

00:02:12.669 --> 00:02:13.810
- What is it?

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:15.963
- There's someone in
my room and it's a boy.

00:02:15.963 --> 00:02:17.580
- (groans) Miles.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:18.670
- [Narrator] Robert Longstreet.

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:20.060
- They had none of that.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:22.300
- If you as a fisherman...

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.600
- Probably ain't my place,

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.100
but maybe she could use

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:28.860
a little time away from the house.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:29.900
- [Narrator] Michael Trucco.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:31.830
- Thought we could all use a refresher.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:33.250
- All right, I'm going
to put my phone down,

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:34.260
reach for my wallet, okay?

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.430
Take it easy.

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:36.380
- [Narrator] Carla Gugino.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:37.510
- It is the sentence of this court

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:38.410
that you be incarcerated

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:39.810
for a period of four to 10 years

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:42.560
in the custody of the Illinois
Department of Corrections.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:43.490
- Can we have a tea party?

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:45.550
- Not now. Young lady?

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:47.630
- Please-o-please?

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:50.063
- No. Come with me right now.

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:54.760
- [Narrator] Fun fact, five
actors from Midnight Mass appear

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:57.370
in Flanagan's next
series, The Midnight Club.

00:02:57.370 --> 00:03:00.610
Zach Gilford, Igby Rigney, Annarah Cymone,

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:03.930
Matt Biedel, Crystal
Balint, and Samantha Sloyan,

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:05.680
which follows terminally ill teens

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:07.923
who meet up to tell scary stories.

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:09.980
- Shit.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:11.030
- [Narrator] The Midnight Club is based

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:12.740
on a book by Christopher Pike.

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:15.530
Pike is also a name used in Midnight Mass.

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:17.060
- Pike.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:18.183
- His name was Pike.

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:21.380
- [Narrator] The haunted
mirror from Flanagan's movie,

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:24.970
Oculus, appears as an Easter
egg in many of his works.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.770
In Midnight Mass, the mirror
is on stage in the rec center

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:30.090
where Riley attends AA meetings.

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:32.780
Flanagan himself makes
a cameo in episode three

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:34.208
and sings in the choir.

00:03:34.208 --> 00:03:35.234
- May I see your permit?

00:03:35.234 --> 00:03:37.320
Where are you going? Right this way.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:39.650
- [Narrator] Composer Andy
Grush, of the Newton brothers

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:40.660
who have composed music

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:43.360
for every Flanagan project since 2013,

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:46.410
appears as the resident
musician of Crockett Island.

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:49.200
Look and listen closely for
more Flanaverse connections

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.343
when you watch Midnight
Mass, only on Netflix.

